{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He said: \"Too slight.\"</b> It is in His eyes, your being a servant to restore Israel to their land by speech." "<b>נְצוּרֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל (preserved ones of Israel).</b> Ruins, like כְּעִיר נְצוּרָה (like a besieged city) (Isaiah 1:8)." "And the meaning: that you shall not restore Israel alone, but I have given you as a light to the nations." "<b>My salvation.</b> To make it heard before it comes to be."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:42.057300128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}